        "geology": "Varied softbottoms - from very shallow sheltered muddy bottoms to deep areas partly anoxic. The deepest site in the Baltic proper, the Landsortsdjupet 459 meters.",
        "hydrology": "Research is focused on marine habitats",
        "soils": "Research is focused on marine habitats",
        "vegetation": "Submerged vegetation and different habitats/biotopes. Highly variable. In shallow bays rather rich vegetation of rooted submerged plant species including Characeans. Rocky bottom from the surface to about 10 meters depth covered with a rich algal community typical for the low salinity of the region.The salinity is about 6 psu. Comments: A wide range of typical habitats and ecosystems are found nearby the station, both very shallow and sheltered and open and wave-exposed sites. A national monitoring program has been running since 1992 studying the open water Station BI), the phytobentos and the soft-bottoms. Further the Himmerfjärden area has been intensively investigated following effects of sewage pollution. The terrestrial environment consists of mixed temperate forests, pastures and meadows. The meadows have been investigated in a national program and the island is a nature reserve and its surrounding waters are a marine reserve since 2001."
      },
