        "operation": {
          "permanent": false,
          "notes": "The staff is employed at Stockholm University but have their working place at the field station, the Askö Laboratory, situated on an island south of Stockholm. The station is managed in close collaboration with the staff, placed at Stockholm University Baltic Sea Centre.\r\nThere is no permanent scientific staff at the Askö Laboratory\r\n",
          "siteVisitInterval": null
        },
        "notes": "At the Askö Laboratory: The facilities are available for research, teaching and monitoring after application for space and resourses. Office space available for guests: 5-10 depending on season.Lab space available for guests: 90- 100 m2 depending e.g. on season and university courses etc. Capacity (nr of flow-through aquaria and sizes):  9 container/tanks á 1.5 m2 , 10 a 600 L and 3 a 3 m2.\r\nFurther facilities: several smaller and larger boats and ships are available as are possibilities for diving and a Remote operated vehcile (ROV). Equippment for sampling and measurement in the field and analysis in the laboratory. Storing facilities, like dry-freezer and -80 C. For details contact the field station and the Stockholm University Baltic Sea homepage http://www.su.se/ostersjocentrum/english/ask%C3%B6-laboratory.",
